WEBVTT

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:34.310
That looks great!

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:36.280
They should be done.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:37.900
Go ahead and start.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:40.070
Let's eat!

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:45.080
<b>Squid Meets Grill?!</b>

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:52.920
This grilled meat is so squidlicious!

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.200
Hey, Squid Girl.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.130
If you think it's good, fine.

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:59.700
If you want to eat a lot, that's fine too.

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:03.080
But stop using your tentacles like that.

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:05.520
Your favorite food is supposed to be shrimp!

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.960
Why are you so stuck on this meat?

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.580
Shrimp goes into a different stomach.

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:11.430
Meat is squidlicious too!

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:14.490
It's important to keep up your 
stamina during the summer.

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:16.080
That's right!

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:18.720
And there's no reason to rush.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:23.330
We've got plenty of sirloin, 
skirt steak, and ribs to go.

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:25.300
Yeah, but...

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:29.290
Sis can really pack away the meat.

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:31.480
That was quick!

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:33.470
It's so good!

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:35.500
Come on, everyone! Dig in.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:37.810
She says dig in,

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:38.470
The next round is done.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.680
but I can't even get a chopstick in.

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:43.440
The meat's all gone...

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:45.580
Then I'll just have to put more on.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:46.640
Hey!

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:48.390
I told you to stop with the tentacles!

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:49.740
Huh?

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:52.030
You're saying I have to eat with my hands?

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:53.580
Of course!

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:55.250
Where are your manners?

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:56.950
You should watch them at the table.

00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:00.380
For me, eating with your 
tentacles is good manners.

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:02.830
That's exactly what I...

00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:04.620
Pipe down, you two.

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:09.620
It's such a waste to argue when 
we've got this delicious dinner.

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:11.750
Yes.

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:11.750
Yes.

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:13.810
This is bad.

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:16.320
The last thing I want to do is piss her off.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:18.380
What if I...

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:23.140
A meal isn't complete with only meat.

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:26.720
Why don't you have some salad as well?

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:29.140
All right, I'm going to 
cook up the next round.

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:31.500
What's wrong with you guys?

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:34.310
You're going to make
 Squid Girl and me overeat!

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:37.230
There's no way I can win this!

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:40.150
I've got to get the ball back in my court!

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:43.110
I get tired of just beef.

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:45.350
Why don't we grill some pork or chicken, too?

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:46.740
Good idea!

00:03:47.170 --> 00:03:49.300
They both just had salad!

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:53.210
Now let them fill their 
stomachs up with this!

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:03.310
You're not eating?

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:06.270
Eat up, Squid Girl.

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:10.390
But... Korean barbecue is all about beef.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:13.480
Say what?!

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:14.840
Yeah, I think so, too.

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:16.610
Go ahead and eat, Eiko.

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:19.190
We'll put some beef on for ourselves next.

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:21.570
Damn it!

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:26.200
Talk about falling into your own trap.

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:29.910
Those ribs look really squiddy good!

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:34.430
Ugh, I'm already full,

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:37.800
but I can't stop now!

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:40.380
I just want to eat some beef!

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:42.210
You're going to gain weight.

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:48.200
Did you know that beef has the 
most calories of all meats?

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:50.820
Oh, I'll be fine!

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:53.020
I'll go jogging once we're done.

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:56.240
Jogging will only increase your muscle mass.

00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:57.980
I guess you're right...

00:04:57.980 --> 00:04:58.810
Yes!

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:00.940
I successfully trapped her!

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:01.870
Now for...

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:07.320
Squid Girl! Stop taking the meat 
out from under my nose!

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:11.270
Why not? You weren't taking it 
and it was just squiding there.

00:05:11.270 --> 00:05:14.810
I wasn't taking it because 
I like it slightly charred.

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:17.420
You're really inconsiderate to this meat!

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:19.780
Get it?

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:25.100
Korean barbecue is not just about 
throwing the meat on the grill.

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:26.710
It's about how you cook the meat:

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:29.790
it's about how far you are willing 
to go to cook the meat!

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:34.580
You must delicately char the outside 
to draw out the aroma of the meat,

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:38.690
coaxing the maximum flavor 
out of each tiny morsel

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:41.940
by burning off the excess fat 
while keeping the juices locked in!

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:43.850
After charring the outside,

00:05:43.850 --> 00:05:47.670
you must grill the meat according to its 
individual fat content and thickness...

00:05:47.670 --> 00:05:49.710
LISTEN TO ME!

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:54.800
Overthinking it makes the 
meat lose its squidlicious flavor.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:59.080
Says the person who has 
no respect for the meat!

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:01.240
If you pile it up on the plate like that,

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:02.960
the last bites will be cold!

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:05.000
You've got to carefully tend to each piece

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:07.610
and eat it while it's still hot!

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:09.880
If you don't want me to take your meat,

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:12.930
why don't you mark your pieces or something?

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:15.720
How am I supposed to do that?

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:17.770
Keep your chopsticks on them.

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:19.790
Then I can't eat anything else!

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:21.370
Mark your territory.

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:22.900
Like how?

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:26.320
Make a squiddle mark like so...

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:30.050
Wai-

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:37.800
You did that on purpose,
 so nobody else could have any!

00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:40.750
No, I just got a squiddle 
irritated by the smoke...

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:42.470
Now we can't eat anymore!

00:06:42.470 --> 00:06:43.590
What are you thinking?!

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:45.320
It's just a little squid ink, it's fine...

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:46.560
It is not fine!

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:48.640
This flavor works.

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:51.200
I can always count on you.

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:52.890
Here, try it!

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:57.060
That's... so... delicious.

00:06:57.730 --> 00:07:01.020
Still, why do I feel like I've lost?

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:04.320
I'm so full!

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:06.190
Thank you!

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:08.030
You're already done?

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:11.910
I left the best cuts for last!

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:16.690
Why did you hold out on us?!

00:07:16.690 --> 00:07:18.910
Because you would have just 
wolfed it down without savoring it.

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:23.670
Indeed, but I'm too full.
 I can't eat anymore.

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:26.580
I would've saved some room, if I had known.

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:27.830
Oh?

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:29.370
That's too bad.

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:32.430
I guess I'll take the responsibility 
and eat it all myself.

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:35.460
You shark!

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:36.940
That's sneaky!

00:07:36.940 --> 00:07:41.000
Oh good, there's still meat left!

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:43.730
I thought I wouldn't get anything...

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:44.980
Oh, no...

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:46.270
We totally forgot...

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:48.030
...about Takeru!

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:53.010
Now that I think about it,
 I'm pretty full, too.

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:56.320
Looks like it's all yours, Takeru!

00:07:56.320 --> 00:07:57.990
Really? This is all for me?

00:07:58.350 --> 00:07:59.160
Are you sure?

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:03.570
That's so good!

00:08:03.570 --> 00:08:06.000
I was really hungry, so it's even better!

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:08.360
We're sorry...

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:10.530
Sorry, Takeru!

00:08:10.530 --> 00:08:11.920
I'm really sorry.

00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:13.100
Huh?

00:08:14.440 --> 00:08:16.930
Why are you all apologizing?

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:21.390
What do you say?

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:23.650
Let's go grab something to drink.

00:08:23.650 --> 00:08:26.260
We'll wait until you're off your shift.

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:29.270
We're sooo considerate!

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:31.540
We're just asking for a 
little bit of your time.

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:32.900
When are you off work?

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:35.580
We'll wait, no matter how long it takes!

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:35.580
I... Sorry.

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:39.430
What are you doing with our waitress?!

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:42.580
Crap, she's trouble!

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:44.890
Catch you later, Ayumi!

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:48.460
Pain in the ass bodyguard.

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:50.460
Who the hell are you calling a bodyguard?

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:53.230
I better not see your 
mugs around here again!

00:08:54.610 --> 00:08:56.550
Ayumi, are you okay?

00:08:57.090 --> 00:08:58.970
Y-Yes.

00:09:00.070 --> 00:09:01.180
What's wrong?

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:06.280
Huh?

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:07.450
Se...

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:08.250
What?

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:09.390
Sel...

00:09:09.390 --> 00:09:10.400
What did you say?

00:09:10.870 --> 00:09:12.350
Self-defense...

00:09:13.770 --> 00:09:16.470
Please... teach me.

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:22.120
<b>Wanna Learn Self-Squidfense?!</b>

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:28.150
I guess since you're really cute 
and quiet, guys would think

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:29.860
you're an easy target.

00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:34.050
I wish I could chase them off like you do.

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:37.140
Well, if you really want to learn 
some self-defense techniques,

00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:38.790
it would be better to talk to...

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:42.590
Squiddie!

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:46.520
Maybe not...

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:49.360
Sis, can't you teach her?

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:51.580
Self-defense, huh?

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:54.290
Well, to nail the enemy's vitals, you...

00:09:54.290 --> 00:09:57.490
Why don't you start much earlier?

00:09:58.330 --> 00:10:00.460
So, like, back to the moment 
when you become aware

00:10:00.460 --> 00:10:01.890
of your assailant's blood thirst?

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:04.300
No, that's even more complicated.

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:09.950
Just something simple, something 
anyone could learn quickly.

00:10:09.950 --> 00:10:12.290
Oh well, in that case...

00:10:15.770 --> 00:10:16.760
Hey!

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:18.590
What the heck are you doing?

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:21.510
I couldn't keep my tentacles back, 
she was wide open.

00:10:22.310 --> 00:10:26.040
It's true, you really are defenseless, Ayumi.

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:28.750
I got it.

00:10:28.750 --> 00:10:31.980
I'm going to help you any way I can!

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:34.230
Really?

00:10:34.740 --> 00:10:38.180
I'll show you an example first.

00:10:38.180 --> 00:10:41.160
Could one of you pretend to be

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:42.960
a hoodlum attacking me?

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:44.540
I can't do that!

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:44.540
I can't do that!

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:47.500
That makes it hard.

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:50.330
Yuigahama Lifeguard Pavilion

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:48.840
What?

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:50.330
You want me to play an attacking hoodlum?

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:51.920
I won't!

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:54.230
That goes against all my ideals about justice,

00:10:54.230 --> 00:10:56.050
even if it is just acting!

00:10:56.500 --> 00:10:58.250
Jeez, he's so stubborn.

00:10:58.250 --> 00:10:59.510
Goro,

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:02.510
this is in the name of a young girl's safety.

00:11:02.920 --> 00:11:04.100
Please!

00:11:04.370 --> 00:11:05.590
All right!

00:11:05.590 --> 00:11:07.460
Jeez, he's so simple.

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:09.310
Squid on.

00:11:09.780 --> 00:11:13.950
If it's to protect another, 
then my duty demands it!

00:11:13.950 --> 00:11:16.440
So, what should I do?

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:18.820
Hmm... well...

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:22.320
I want you to attack me with all you've got!

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:27.290
To attack you... with all... I've got?!

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:32.790
But, but, but.... there's something 
not quite right about that...

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:36.880
Don't worry. 
This is just practice.

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:40.340
I see.

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:43.550
This is practice for protecting people.

00:11:43.890 --> 00:11:47.350
If anything, attacking Chizuru right now 
is the only morally right act!

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:50.270
I have to, for the world, for mankind!

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:53.940
I have no sinister feelings at all!

00:11:55.590 --> 00:11:56.570
I'm sorry!

00:11:58.530 --> 00:11:59.240
Huh?

00:12:03.730 --> 00:12:05.760
What just happened?!

00:12:06.220 --> 00:12:09.330
It looked like Goro just fell over by himself.

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:11.330
You are so strong!

00:12:12.570 --> 00:12:15.870
Actually, I didn't use strength at all.

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:16.670
Huh?

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:19.110
Even an ordinary girl like myself

00:12:19.110 --> 00:12:21.830
can bring down a much bigger enemy

00:12:21.830 --> 00:12:24.590
by using their own strength against them.

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:26.320
Did she say she was...

00:12:26.320 --> 00:12:27.350
...an ordinary girl?

00:12:31.320 --> 00:12:35.900
That looks way too complicated 
for someone like me.

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:38.690
It's easy, once you get the hang of it.

00:12:39.310 --> 00:12:41.030
It was just for a moment...

00:12:41.470 --> 00:12:43.540
but she touched me.

00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:45.680
I think.

00:12:46.100 --> 00:12:47.450
Goro...

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:48.950
Are you all right?

00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:51.200
I tried to hold back a little,

00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:54.490
but if you're not up to playing 
the assailant, you can-

00:12:54.490 --> 00:12:55.580
I'm up to it!

00:12:56.150 --> 00:12:59.550
Please let me help!

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:33.770
Hey!

00:13:33.770 --> 00:13:34.880
Hi, Gramps.

00:13:34.880 --> 00:13:37.600
Looks like you're done for the day.

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:39.670
Yeah, we're just wrapping up.

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:43.550
Well, we don't close until later 
and we're short on staff.

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:44.300
Ayumi...

00:13:46.770 --> 00:13:48.460
Inkredible!

00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:51.470
Looks like you've got 
that self-defense down!

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:54.980
Huh? D-dad!

00:13:55.370 --> 00:13:59.640
I guess my daughter has finally 
entered the rebellious stage.

00:13:59.640 --> 00:14:00.830
N-no!

00:14:00.830 --> 00:14:02.690
It was the training...

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:06.430
It means you can react reflexively now!

00:14:06.430 --> 00:14:08.660
Chizuru is a very good teacher,

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:10.370
but you've really made 
oceans of progress, Ayumi!

00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:14.040
Where is Ayumi's teacher?

00:14:19.230 --> 00:14:23.960
That's why I told you to not overdo it.

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:26.360
Oh, no, I'm sorry... ouch.

00:14:27.750 --> 00:14:30.350
Chizuru's nursing me back to health.

00:14:30.900 --> 00:14:33.400
This is pure happiness!

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:43.020
This sure is a nice day.

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:46.870
The weather's so good, there 
aren't even any customers.

00:14:46.870 --> 00:14:49.240
There's not a single squidding person on the beach.

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:51.280
It really is too hot.

00:14:51.920 --> 00:14:54.220
Maybe we should just close for the day.

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:58.210
Just leave it to us!

00:14:58.390 --> 00:15:03.210
<b>Aren't You Freezing Your Tentacles Off?!</b>

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:08.610
Wow, that's really cool!

00:15:08.610 --> 00:15:12.970
It's a high-powered cooling system that 
works with an internal battery.

00:15:13.270 --> 00:15:15.880
That feels good.

00:15:16.340 --> 00:15:19.360
It's as comfortable as it is in the spring.

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:20.700
Indeed.

00:15:21.370 --> 00:15:23.940
But it's totally pointless!

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:25.030
You're right.

00:15:25.030 --> 00:15:27.790
It doesn't matter if the customers 
don't know we have this.

00:15:27.790 --> 00:15:30.110
Let's turn up the cooling!

00:15:33.260 --> 00:15:35.620
Feels like a cool breeze is blowing in here!

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:36.990
Can I come in for a bit?

00:15:37.350 --> 00:15:39.280
It's just Goro.

00:15:39.280 --> 00:15:41.690
Here I thought we had a real customer.

00:15:41.690 --> 00:15:43.130
How am I not a real customer?!

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:47.760
But it looks like you 
guys finally got an A/C.

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:50.920
Can you feel it, even out there?

00:15:50.920 --> 00:15:53.670
You sure can! Perfectly!

00:15:53.670 --> 00:15:58.250
Then again, I noticed since I was 
patrolling the area right here.

00:15:58.250 --> 00:16:01.480
I don't think you can feel it, 
unless you come really close.

00:16:02.860 --> 00:16:05.400
If anything... it feels 
a little too cold now.

00:16:05.670 --> 00:16:07.760
If you want to complain, get out.

00:16:07.760 --> 00:16:08.860
Agreed.

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:12.160
Fine, I'll go back to work.

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:13.200
Bye.

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:17.160
I guess that means this isn't enough.

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:20.700
It's really hot today.

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:23.920
That club room was like a sauna.

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:26.560
I want to go home and take a shower.

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:29.630
It feels cool right here.

00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:32.280
Look at that!

00:16:36.320 --> 00:16:38.430
Excuse me?

00:16:38.690 --> 00:16:40.260
Welcome!

00:16:40.260 --> 00:16:42.640
Why is this the only 
place where it's winter?

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:44.030
Nice and cool, huh?

00:16:44.030 --> 00:16:45.860
Want to come in?

00:16:45.860 --> 00:16:49.020
This isn't just cool anymore, 
it's downright cold!

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:53.200
Don't worry, we've got some 
winter coats just for that!

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:55.910
I... see.

00:16:56.430 --> 00:16:57.870
What do you say?

00:16:57.870 --> 00:17:01.450
With this high-powered 
artificial snow machine,

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:04.080
you can enjoy winter any time of the year!

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:07.010
I didn't think those jellyfish could make it snow.

00:17:07.010 --> 00:17:08.500
Hey, Squid Girlie!

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:10.560
Let's make a snowman!

00:17:10.560 --> 00:17:12.050
A what-man?

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:14.510
You mean someone who 
squidverses with the spirits?

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:18.960
You don't know "snowman," 
but you know "shaman"?

00:17:19.650 --> 00:17:25.310
To make a snowman, 
you gotta make a big one of these!

00:17:25.740 --> 00:17:30.190
What's so squidciting about doing
 something like that in the cold?

00:17:30.810 --> 00:17:32.050
Oh.

00:17:32.050 --> 00:17:35.960
Here I was thinking you could 
make a snowman so magnificent

00:17:35.960 --> 00:17:37.660
that no human could imitate you.

00:17:39.110 --> 00:17:40.900
Well, when you put it like that,

00:17:40.900 --> 00:17:43.100
I guess I have no choice 
 but to show you humans

00:17:43.100 --> 00:17:44.370
how to make a real squidman!

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:46.000
Yay!

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:48.960
I guess Takeru's learned 
how to manipulate her.

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:54.920
Done!

00:17:55.180 --> 00:17:56.520
Wow!

00:17:56.520 --> 00:17:57.990
That's huge!

00:17:57.990 --> 00:17:59.350
Now it's just missing eyes and a mouth!

00:17:59.730 --> 00:18:01.180
Leave it to me!

00:18:04.940 --> 00:18:06.230
So what do you say?

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:09.530
You pathetic humans could never 
make a squidman like this!

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:13.860
Man, I saw something I didn't want to see.

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:17.610
If you made it bigger, 
you could make it into a snow hut.

00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:19.620
Nice idea!

00:18:20.600 --> 00:18:24.830
A snow hut? Is that like a Buddha statue?

00:18:28.070 --> 00:18:31.580
What kind of freak weather is this?

00:18:38.950 --> 00:18:40.930
What are you doing in there?!

00:18:41.570 --> 00:18:43.490
Hey, Cindy!

00:18:43.490 --> 00:18:44.440
Can't you see?

00:18:44.440 --> 00:18:46.260
We're having a hot pot meal!

00:18:46.280 --> 00:18:51.070
It's been so hot, it seems like 
this summer has lasted over a year,

00:18:51.070 --> 00:18:53.900
so we were starting to miss 
this nice cold weather.

00:18:54.250 --> 00:18:57.030
You're going to get sick dressed like that.

00:18:58.520 --> 00:19:01.050
Don't you have something more substantial?

00:19:01.050 --> 00:19:04.520
That's the last coat we have, sorry.

00:19:04.520 --> 00:19:07.290
Why don't you eat with us?

00:19:10.100 --> 00:19:11.830
That was delicious!

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:15.250
Yup, there's nothing like 
a hot pot on a cold day!

00:19:15.770 --> 00:19:18.590
Don't you think it's getting 
a squiddle too cold though?

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:23.050
What's wrong, Squid Girl?

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:25.630
It's squidpletely white out there!

00:19:26.650 --> 00:19:28.230
I'm worried about the restaurant.

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:29.790
Let's hurry back!

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:34.620
I can't see anything at all.

00:19:34.620 --> 00:19:36.690
Are we going the right way?

00:19:37.370 --> 00:19:39.950
I'm starting to feel sleepy.

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:42.410
Squiddie! You can't fall asleep!

00:19:43.310 --> 00:19:44.230
This is it...

00:19:44.230 --> 00:19:46.160
I can't go any further.

00:19:46.850 --> 00:19:47.830
I see it!

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:49.290
It's the Lemon!

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:50.470
Someone, open up!

00:19:50.470 --> 00:19:51.750
We're dying out here!

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:53.630
Squiddie, wake up!

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:56.470
It's like we're really stranded in a blizzard.

00:19:56.470 --> 00:19:59.850
Hey, you can get in the back!

00:19:59.850 --> 00:20:01.760
Good job, Takeru!

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:04.180
Hey, three stooges, what's going on here?!

00:20:04.570 --> 00:20:07.350
The control mechanism is broken.

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:09.740
It's got a mind of its own.

00:20:09.740 --> 00:20:12.350
Looks like this test run was a failure!

00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:17.400
Don't test that stuff on our restaurant!

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:19.820
Hurry up and repair it!

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:22.680
We have no way of knowing

00:20:22.680 --> 00:20:25.390
where the machine is, exactly,
 in this snow storm.

00:20:25.390 --> 00:20:26.780
What?!

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:31.160
Weird, there are shrimp 
swimming in this place.

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:33.920
Pull yourself together, Squiddie!

00:20:34.600 --> 00:20:36.790
I'm going to die. 
I'm really going to die.

00:20:37.610 --> 00:20:39.570
Everyone's at the end of their ropes.

00:20:39.570 --> 00:20:42.340
Well, can't you at least do 
something about the cold?!

00:20:42.340 --> 00:20:44.380
Well, not really...

00:20:45.280 --> 00:20:47.350
That reminds me!

00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:50.610
This high-powered cooling 
system has a heating system

00:20:50.610 --> 00:20:53.200
for times just like these!

00:20:53.200 --> 00:20:55.270
Oh, yeah!

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:58.980
Just call it an A/C.

00:21:01.700 --> 00:21:03.780
It's gotten warmer.

00:21:04.800 --> 00:21:07.640
I can feel the life coming back into me.

00:21:07.640 --> 00:21:09.910
I was really getting worried back there.

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:12.150
Now we're all safe.

00:21:15.270 --> 00:21:18.240
But is anyone else getting warm?

00:21:18.240 --> 00:21:19.880
Can you turn the heat down a bit?

00:21:20.200 --> 00:21:21.670
No can do.

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:23.230
The remote control's battery died,

00:21:23.230 --> 00:21:24.680
so we can't change the temperature any more.

00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:25.790
Huh?

00:21:27.100 --> 00:21:28.510
It's so hot!

00:21:28.510 --> 00:21:30.720
Why is it so hot in here?

00:21:29.070 --> 00:21:29.740
Sanae?

00:21:29.740 --> 00:21:30.720
Nagatsuki?

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:35.120
Did you walk through that 
snow storm dressed in that?!

00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:36.650
What are you talking about?

00:21:36.890 --> 00:21:38.950
It's really hot out there.

00:21:38.950 --> 00:21:39.650
Huh?

00:21:39.650 --> 00:21:43.160
What are you guys doing dressed like that?

00:21:43.160 --> 00:21:45.060
Is this some test of endurance?

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:54.320
Screw winter!

00:21:54.320 --> 00:21:57.040
Summer is the squidding best!

00:21:59.850 --> 00:22:02.420
It's been a scorching hot day across Japan,

00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:05.180
but here in Okinawa,
 the snow is coming down!

00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:06.880
<b>Natural Disaster?!</b>

00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:06.880
<b>Snow in Okinawa in the Middle of Summer</b>

00:22:05.500 --> 00:22:07.830
This unprecedented weather is

00:22:07.830 --> 00:22:09.930
a historical first since records began...

00:23:40.700 --> 00:23:44.610
Hello. My name is Kiyomi Sakura.
 I'm the vice president of the Invasion Club.

00:23:44.610 --> 00:23:45.190
Next up are:

00:23:45.190 --> 00:23:46.650
Squidn't that hypnosis?!

00:23:46.650 --> 00:23:47.690
Shall we join tentacles?!

00:23:47.690 --> 00:23:49.400
I ink we're alone now?!

00:23:49.780 --> 00:23:53.480
We'll continue to do our best with the club,
 so please support us.
